From ed1df5779b17bccf1c93ed0ba4509b7b422abad4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add "Mute Channel For..." submenu to the channel header
 menu

The channel header dropdown gets a "Mute Channel For..." submenu with
1 hour, 8 hours, 24 hours and "Until I unmute" options, shown while the
channel isn't muted. On mobile it opens in the usual submenu modal.

When a channel is muted for a limited time, the "Unmute Channel" item
shows how long is left (e.g. "Unmutes in 7 hours and 13 minutes"),
refreshing while the menu is open. The existing mute toggle now goes
through muteChannel/unmuteChannel so that toggling clears any pending
expiry.

The desktop dropdown measures its width so the submenu can open next to
it, and MenuItemAction's extraText now accepts a node so the remaining
time can be a FormattedMessage.
